---
code: predict-out-of-dialect
when-fires: a check function body uses a construct outside the check dialect (a strict subset of sh). oracle/predict.rs lift_failure.
why: out-of-dialect input is a lift failure. PASSTHROUGH — the check parser's description rides `detail`.
edit-loop: edit a sentence in the transcript below, then run `mise run loom:compile -- predict-out-of-dialect && mise run loom:promote -- predict-out-of-dialect`. `mise run loom:vars -- --all predict-out-of-dialect` lists this case's values; type {{name}} to insert or move one.
---
-- oracle.sh --
# dorc-lang/v0.2
pkg__is_converged() { [ "`dpkg -s "$1"`" = installed ]; }

-- replay --
$ dorc lint oracle.sh --no-tools
dorc lint findings (advisory; the machine format `--format=jsonl` is the stable surface):

oracle.sh:
  warning[oracle-role-fn-unlifted]: [unwritten: oracle-role-fn-unlifted]
        [ oracle.sh:2:1
     2 | pkg__is_converged() { [ "`dpkg -s "$1"`" = installed ]; }
       | \_______________/
  error[predict-out-of-dialect]: sm statement does not start with a word
        [ oracle.sh:2:23
     2 | pkg__is_converged() { [ "`dpkg -s "$1"`" = installed ]; }
       |                       ^

dorc lint: 1 error, 1 warning, 0 infos across 1 file.
